    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0320" n="308" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg308"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10405: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-27T23:00:00+02:00">April 27, 1941—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 27—10:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>220. To be communicated to the President. For the week ending April 26, the most
                    important events and conditions here are as follows:</p>
                <p>(1) The strong belief of all sources hitherto reliable is that following the
                    conquest of Yugoslavia and Greece, Turkey will do what Germany wants her to
                    do.</p>
                <p>The turning over by Germany of Thrace, and Grecian and Yugoslavian Macedonia to
                    Bulgaria to administer.</p>
                <p>While German troops have almost completely overrun Europe she has only occupied
                    countries hating her intensely and half-hearted and unwarlike allies to count
                    on.</p>
                <pb facs="0321" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>
                <p>The Bulgarians are an intensely practical people. German propaganda has magnified
                    in their eyes the new territory given them until they are now wholeheartedly
                    with Germany. They now think of the Bulgaria of a thousand years ago reborn. I
                    am forming the impression, and every day it is stronger, that Germany will take
                    this hard-bitten and grateful Bulgarian people and use them as a nucleus to
                    build a powerful nation, strongly equipped with the most modern and mechanized
                    weapons whom Germany can depend upon to guard for her southeastern Europe.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
